{"ts":"2026-08-05T11:55:51.273Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["readauthoritativerows-typed-outcome","unavailable-authority-defers-typed","contradictory-replica-dbs-detected-conflicting","no-cross-node-clobber-on-conflict"]}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["readauthoritativerows-typed-outcome","unavailable-authority-defers-typed"]}},{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["contradictory-replica-dbs-detected-conflicting","no-cross-node-clobber-on-conflict"]}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"Once durable cluster identity exists, the raw union over every nodes-p* replica file is replaced by a small local membership manifest (or, at minimum, contradictory replica DBs are treated as conflicting rather than unioned), and readAuthoritativeRows returns a typed {state, rows} outcome so that an unavailable authority defers rejoin instead of silently collapsing to the fresh path with a downgraded row. doneWhen: the test-receipt probe reads solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json with outstanding 0 — typed-outcome and conflict-detection receipts passing (deterministic red-on-revert evidence harness).","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"depends-on-cluster-identity","statement":"This Quest consumes the durable cluster_id minted by durable-cluster-identity; the membership manifest and conflict detection key on cluster identity, so it must not be started before that Quest's mint-and-persist frontier lands."},{"id":"unavailable-authority-defers","statement":"readAuthoritativeRows must distinguish missing/readable/unavailable; transient authority unavailability defers rejoin with a typed deferred outcome (not silent absence), so the durable-rejoin fast path is not silently defeated and the row is not downgraded to JOINING with a fresh created_at."},{"id":"no-cross-node-clobber","statement":"The fall-through from an unavailable authority must remain a serialized, self-keyed, retry-wrapped upsert that throws on real unavailability; the typed outcome must not introduce a path that can clobber another node's row."},{"id":"red-on-revert","statement":"Each new regression test must fail when the typed-outcome or conflict-detection mechanism is reverted while the rest of the change remains."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"frontierIds":["authoritative-rows-typed-outcome","replica-evidence-conflict-detection"]}}
{"ts":"2026-08-05T11:56:07.126Z","type":"attempt","frontier":"authoritative-rows-typed-outcome","rung":"observe","rungIndex":0,"prevRungIndex":0,"hypothesis":"Frontier 1 (authoritative-rows-typed-outcome): readAuthoritativeRows no longer collapses missing/unavailable/failed to a bare []. It returns a typed {state, rows} outcome (AUTHORITATIVE_ROW_READ_STATE) distinguishing READABLE from UNAVAILABLE; an unavailable authority throws a typed deferred retryable error (deferRetry + retryAfterMs) that the wrapped-error carrier propagates so the join retries, with zero upsertJoinNode calls (no fresh clobber). The existing serialized self-keyed retry-wrapped upsert is untouched. New red-on-revert suite (4 tests, 16 assertions); reverting readAuthoritativeRows to bare-array fails 12 assertions.","changeRef":"diff:solve/changes/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2/attempt-1.diff.json","metricBefore":0,"metricAfter":0,"metricDirection":"lower-is-better","invalidSample":false,"baselineAbsent":false,"done":true,"evidence":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","beforeEvidence":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","beforeEvidenceIdentity":{"path":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","resolvedPath":"/media/peter/4509da27-4751-4dee-b366-f3983d0777252/peter/projects/lagrange/solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","exists":true,"size":928,"mtimeMs":1785930938685.0874,"sha256":"e7c4bebc1741e44ec4817084233f5fdfe0695336d37695a86b61d56f180f43b5","probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["readauthoritativerows-typed-outcome","unavailable-authority-defers-typed"]},"observedAt":"2026-08-05T11:55:51.277Z","fingerprint":"8fe5fd3e2d7a8433e580eadf9365ad30444cb1050bd8afc49f729cb58e29925a"},"beforeEvidenceFingerprint":"8fe5fd3e2d7a8433e580eadf9365ad30444c